WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.860
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:02.970
happening all the time,

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.010
so we gathered some of
the most-hyped products

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.450
to test for ourselves.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:08.085
I finally got my hands on

00:00:08.085 --> 00:00:10.680
the Haus Labs Atomic Shake lip lacquer.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.630
This is another one of
those transfer-proof

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.220
glossy lipsticks.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.680
This is definitely the
hot new lip formula.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.440
So, you shake the product
well, then apply it.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.990
The pigment in this really shocked me.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.930
It was so vibrant, it almost looked neon.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.370
This went on so smooth,

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.710
I didn't need more than one
layer for full coverage,

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.420
and it was so glossy.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.890
I had to wait 15 seconds

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.140
for what they call the
"shine shield" to form.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:35.550
Then I kissed the back of my hand

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.580
to see if I got any transfer, and nothing.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.770
I've tried three lipsticks
with this kind of formula,

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.480
and so far, this is the best one.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.600
This is the Modelones Color
Cube in Bonfire Amour.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.520
It's a solid gel cream palette.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.170
It comes with nine gel polishes,

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.090
and you can get them in
different color stories

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.170
and finishes.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.150
It also comes with this little brush.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.250
I've used a solid gel cream before,

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.530
but I forgot how thick it actually is,

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.070
so it did take me some time
to apply it in even layers.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.262
I did have to do two coats

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:05.170
for full coverage on some colors.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.470
I think a product like this
can be super convenient,

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.020
especially if you do nail art
or just don't have the space

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:12.240
to keep a bunch of gel polishes around.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.980
It doesn't come with a base or topcoat,

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.810
but I still really like this.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.870
I tested out a ton of
products from Jason Wu Beauty.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:20.100
This is a new brand for me,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.170
so let's start with what I didn't like.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:25.260
This Free-Da Brow was too light
for me, which is my fault,

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.270
but the formula on this is weird.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:30.090
It feels like an oily cream
that never dries down,

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.400
so I doubt it'll keep my brows in place.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.800
These Stay in Line lip
liners weren't great.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.240
They were also too light for me,

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.030
so I ended up using my own
lip liner to deepen it.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.340
These are smooth but a little too creamy.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.465
They don't feel like they're going to

00:01:42.465 --> 00:01:44.670
last very long on the lips at all.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.980
I also didn't like the Wu-Prime Eye.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.010
The formula is so tacky and thick.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:53.040
It made my eye shadow look
patchy in certain areas.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.230
Now on to the stuff I loved.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:58.350
This Flora 4 palette was
surprisingly pigmented

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.580
and easy to blend.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:01.557
I feel like the primer
is what got in the way

00:02:01.557 --> 00:02:03.240
of showing you its full potential,

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.100
but I still really liked it.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.320
This blush trio is so gorgeous

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.940
and blended out really nicely.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.360
I used this Ready to Shimmer
cream shadow as a highlighter,

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.610
and it gave me the prettiest golden glow,

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.890
even though it's not
really meant for the face.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:18.990
This Jewel Stick was incredible.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:21.150
Look how much it brightened
up my inner corners.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.320
The Honey Fluff lip cream

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.693
was soft and comfortable on the lips.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.380
If you get anything from this brand,

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.750
get this Extra Pout lip plumper.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.399
Oh, my God. Even if you don't care

00:02:32.399 --> 00:02:33.810
about the lip-plumping aspect,

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.880
this is one of the best lip-gloss formulas

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.170
I have ever tried.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.810
It's so cushiony and shiny and amazing,

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:41.340
and everyone should get it.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.860
The Make Up For Ever The
Professionall Mascara

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.260
is ... definitely a mascara.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:47.460
It's nothing amazing.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.930
It has one side for lifting

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.910
and the other side for volumizing.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.200
I didn't get much of a lift,

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.330
but I did get a nice amount of volume.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.130
I just think there are
better mascaras out there

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:57.270
for way less money.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:59.220
I am a huge fan of About-Face.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.840
I love so many of its products.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.000
So when these Cheek Freak
blush balms dropped,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.250
I snatched up three different colors.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.483
I'm just gonna say it.

00:03:06.483 --> 00:03:09.066
I am so in love with these.

00:03:09.066 --> 00:03:10.470
I was nervous at first

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.630
because it's described as a "blush balm,"

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:15.810
which to me sounded like it
would break up my foundation,

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:18.480
but these blended in so beautifully.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.130
It never moved the product underneath,

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.230
even if my skin was already powdered,

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.300
and the pigment on these is unreal.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.490
You can build them up
however much you want.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:29.160
I think these can work for
so many different skin tones.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.990
They are so, so good.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:33.120
I made the horrible mistake of purchasing

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.960
the Winky Lux Saucy Gloss
four-piece combo lip-gloss set.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.660
This was made in
collaboration with Applebee's,

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.690
and the glosses are
inspired by its wing sauces.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:45.210
You guys, I thought
everyone was exaggerating

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:48.750
when they said the smell
was making them gag, but no.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:51.720
These smell God-awful, and it sucks so bad

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.060
because the color story is so pretty.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:56.400
And I could see this concept working

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.940
had they just not added the sauce scents,

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.530
or even if they did something like,

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:03.330
lemon pepper smells like lemon,

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.640
Buffalo is just a spicy lip plumper.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.950
But no, they went in this direction.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.720
We all bought it and talked about it,

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.370
which is probably what they wanted.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.680
So I hope you're happy, Winky Lux.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.350
You ruined four beautiful glosses.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.570
I tried out a new foundation from Chanel.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.760
I actually wouldn't
call this a foundation.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.270
It's more like a
super-hydrating, light tint.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:27.210
It's very similar to that
Rose Inc tinted serum

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:28.680
I tried a while ago.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.050
So it has these pigment beads that burst

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:32.880
and spread as you apply it.

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.700
This literally feels
like nothing on the skin.

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.020
There is little coverage,

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.410
but it evens everything out
nicely and it feels hydrating.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.540
I don't think this has
a strong staying power,

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.770
but it's still a pretty tint

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:45.840
for when you don't want to do too much.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.060
Chanel also has a blush in this formula,

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.710
so I tested that out too.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.900
I actually blended it out
on the back of my hand

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.420
before applying and tapped
it on with a sponge.

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:56.010
It took a minute to build up the color,

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.440
but I think it's supposed
to look very natural.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.810
It also didn't break up
the product underneath.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.850
I'm surprised by how much I liked these.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:03.780
They don't do too much,

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.610
but it's enough to make a difference.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.460
This is the Maybelline Shadow
Blocks Eyeshadow Palette.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:10.230
It's a tiny stack of eye shadows,

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:13.170
very similar to the Kaja bento trios.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.940
The packaging is pretty cheap.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:17.160
One of my shadows fell out, but it's OK.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:18.930
I applied these without any primer

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:21.060
just to see how they perform on their own.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.430
They're actually pretty pigmented shadows.

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:24.870
I didn't have any trouble blending them,

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.370
and the shimmer shade was pretty,

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.470
but overall I think these are just OK.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.210
I like the idea of a palette like this

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:31.740
more than the execution.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.920
Everyone has been loving
these NYX Jumbo Lash lashes,

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.090
so I had to try them

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:38.640
even though I am terrible
with false lashes.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:40.050
I thought the style Ego Flare

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:42.630
would look nice on my eye
shape, and I was right.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:45.185
These lashes made me feel
like a whole new person.

00:05:45.185 --> 00:05:47.370
Like, these are Disney princess eyes.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:48.764
They were pretty easy to apply,

00:05:48.764 --> 00:05:50.400
and the band was really comfortable.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.110
I think these have totally convinced me

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:53.730
to wear lashes more often.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:56.700
This is the Urban Decay
24/7 Moondust Shadow

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:58.170
in Space Cowboy.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.360
This is basically a glitter shadow.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.700
This shade in particular
has been going viral.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:05.310
It is super intense and reflective,

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:08.130
but you can definitely
diffuse it to be more subtle.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:10.560
This formula is really
smooth and easy to work with

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:13.560
however you want to use
it, so I really loved this.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:14.970
I did get some glitter fallout,

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.470
so I'd recommend using a primer

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:19.410
or leaving some powder under
the eyes while you're applying.

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:21.180
If you want something more eye-catching

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.003
and elevated than a shimmer
shadow, this is perfect.

